&lt;p&gt;The candidate will join Dataiku&#39;s brand and creative team as our motion design apprentice, working on animated content that shows up everywhere our brand does: product videos, interviews, demos, social video, digital ads, internal communications, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will start by supporting our lead motion designer on projects and will help complete them by owning certain pieces end to end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce animations, video edits and visual effects for campaigns, events and social channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt existing formats across platforms and aspect ratios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build storyboards and animatics, then take them through to final render&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with brand designers, content, product and field marketers to turn briefs into impactful video assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep productions consistent with the Dataiku visual identity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A student currently enrolled in a design, motion or audiovisual program, seeking a 1 or 2 year apprenticeship (4 days per week; at least 2-3 days in Paris office each week would be ideal).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of After Effects and Premiere Pro. Bonus if you’ve worked with Runway or Higgsfield. We don&#39;t expect mastery, we expect the candidate to be able to build something and improve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail (timing, kerning on titles, export settings).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about graphic design, AI, and art beyond motion specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who asks questions when a creative brief submitted by a colleague in the business has gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working English, written and spoken.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What the apprenticeship offers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of how motion design works inside a brand system rather than as one-off pieces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production workflow on high-stakes deliverables with real deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practice giving and receiving feedback on creative work without it becoming personal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentoring from our senior motion designer, plus exposure to the wider brand and marketing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with AI tools such as Midjourney, Runway, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound design or music editing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making content for a tech or B2B audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Figma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apprenticeship contract (alternance), 1 or 2 years, starting October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in Paris,&amp;nbsp; 2-3 days/week on site. Ability to work remotely on other days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;To apply&lt;/span&gt;: send CV and portfolio/showreel/website (schoolwork included)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
